# Python bytecode from the CI check scripts in .github/scripts/.
# Importing one of them (or pytest touching them) writes __pycache__ next to the
# source, and a `git add -A` then sweeps it in. Two .pyc files reached this
# branch that way before this file existed.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# Collector output. Tatar.ps1 and linux/tatar-linux.sh write a timestamped
# evidence directory; none of it belongs in the repo, and some of it would be
# real evidence from whatever host it was run on.
*_20[0-9][0-9]-[0-9][0-9]-[0-9][0-9]_*/
tatar.log
summary.json
TATAR_Report_*.txt
manifest_sha256.txt
chain_of_custody.txt

# Editor / OS noise
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
*~
.idea/
.vscode/
